    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it just feels like a lot of \"potential\" savings and \"long-term\" stuff vs. the very real, immediate cost of staying in business. if a small factory has to spend its entire profit margin on new equipment just to meet a new standard, they might not even be around long enough to see those \"efficiencies\" kick in. isn't it a bit risky to assume that these regulations are actually net-positive for the economy when they hit small players so hard?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
