      "content": "You are correct that the initial capital burden can be an existential threat to smaller, less capitalized businesses right now. This \"upfront cost vs. long-term gain\" dynamic is the core economic debate around these regulations. Proponents argue the long-term stability of the environment and a more advanced industrial base is the \"net positive,\" while critics emphasize the very real risk of immediate firm failure for the smallest players without targeted support.",
